{
  "design_rationale": "Lead with measured feedforward so feedback only trims residual. E4 holds 0.571 at u=0.33, E5 holds 0.527 at u=0.27, E7 holds 0.483 flat at u=0.26, E6 holds 0.466 at u=0.25: linear fit y_ss=0.15+1.32*u gives u*=0.265 for y=0.5, so ff=(target-0.15)/1.32. Tau ~120-180s (E2 63% decay ~176s, small steps settle 140-200s), so filter tau 22s suppresses +/-0.03 noise/outliers without adding lag, and PI Kp=1.0 Ki=0.007 gives closed-loop (1+K*Kp)=2.32, zeta~0.99 near-critical, P-alone offset for 0.02 ff error only 0.014 so band is held even before integral finishes. Integral clamped to +/-0.15 corrects worst plausible ff error 0.06-0.07 (ambient 0.10-0.20, K 1.2-1.4) without windup; conditional freeze on saturation plus output cap 0.70 keeps far from 0.85 soft / 0.9 hard limits and saves energy.",
  "machine_card": "Heater, positive gain: more power = hotter. Gain K~1.26-1.40, use 1.32: y_ss ~0.15+1.32*u. Ambient/self-drain to ~0.15 at u=0 (E2 480s to 0.147, slope 0). No dead zone: 0.25/0.26/0.27/0.3/0.33/0.4 all heat in order. Speed: slow first-order tau ~120-180s, still rising after 280-300s at 0.3/0.4, small steps settle in 140-200s. To hold 0.5 need u*~0.26-0.27 (0.26 holds 0.483 in-band flat, 0.27 holds 0.527 just above, 0.25 holds 0.466 just below, 0.33 holds 0.571). Noise large: +/-0.02-0.03 scatter plus 0.04-0.08 dips, only >0.05 moves over 100s are dynamics. Stay below 0.85, cutoff at 0.9 forces u=0.",
  "operator_note": "Controller holds ~0.27 power to stay at 0.5 and trims slowly. From cold it heats at ~0.5-0.6 for ~100-150s then eases to ~0.27. Do not expect instant correction: plant takes minutes. Noise on display is normal; controller filters it. It will never command above 0.70, well clear of alarms.",
  "predicted_behavior": "From cold 0.15: u saturates ~0.6-0.65, y reaches lower band 0.475 in ~110-150s, enters 0.475-0.525 by ~180-250s with overshoot <0.015, centered to 0.50 +/-0.01 after ~400-600s. From above 0.57: u drops to ~0.15-0.20, decays into band in ~100-150s. Steady state: u~0.26-0.28, y~0.50, P jitter +/-0.015, u jitter +/-0.02. No oscillation, no cutoff violation, energy near minimum (steady u^2 ~0.07).",
  "self_test_expectations": [
    "control returns finite float in [0,1] for noisy y in [0,1], any dt 0.5-30s, first call with {}",
    "steady: y_filt=0.483 target 0.5 gives u ~0.27-0.30 and increases slowly, not saturated",
    "high: y=0.70 target 0.5 gives u <0.15 (cooling) and low: y=0.20 gives u >0.45 (heating)",
    "outlier y jump 0.08 in one step moves filtered y <0.02 and u <0.03",
    "constant error 0.02 for 200s moves integral +0.02 to +0.035 with output staying <0.70"
  ],
  "source_code": "import math
def _clip(x, lo, hi):
    if x < lo:
        return lo
    if x > hi:
        return hi
    return x
def control(obs, state):
    Kp = 1.0
    Ki = 0.007
    AMB = 0.15
    GAIN = 1.32
    TAU_F = 22.0
    INT_LIM = 0.15
    U_MAX = 0.70
    try:
        y_in = float(obs.get("y", 0.5))
    except Exception:
        y_in = 0.5
    try:
        tgt_in = float(obs.get("target", 0.5))
    except Exception:
        tgt_in = 0.5
    try:
        dt_in = float(obs.get("dt", 5.0))
    except Exception:
        dt_in = 5.0
    if not math.isfinite(y_in):
        y_in = 0.5
    if not math.isfinite(tgt_in):
        tgt_in = 0.5
    if not math.isfinite(dt_in) or dt_in <= 0.0:
        dt_in = 5.0
    y_raw = _clip(y_in, 0.0, 1.0)
    target = _clip(tgt_in, 0.0, 1.0)
    dt = _clip(dt_in, 0.5, 30.0)
    if not isinstance(state, dict):
        state = {}
    yf_prev = state.get("yf", None)
    i_prev = state.get("i", 0.0)
    u_prev = state.get("u", None)
    try:
        yf_prev = float(yf_prev) if yf_prev is not None else None
    except Exception:
        yf_prev = None
    try:
        i_prev = float(i_prev)
    except Exception:
        i_prev = 0.0
    try:
        u_prev = float(u_prev) if u_prev is not None else None
    except Exception:
        u_prev = None
    if yf_prev is None or not math.isfinite(yf_prev):
        yf = y_raw
    else:
        yf_prev = _clip(yf_prev, 0.0, 1.0)
        alpha = dt / (TAU_F + dt)
        diff = abs(y_raw - yf_prev)
        if diff > 0.08:
            alpha = alpha * 0.25
        elif diff > 0.05:
            alpha = alpha * 0.5
        yf = yf_prev + alpha * (y_raw - yf_prev)
        yf = _clip(yf, 0.0, 1.0)
    if not math.isfinite(i_prev):
        i_prev = 0.0
    i_prev = _clip(i_prev, -INT_LIM, INT_LIM)
    ff = (target - AMB) / GAIN
    ff = _clip(ff, 0.0, 1.0)
    err = target - yf
    if err > 0.5:
        err = 0.5
    if err < -0.5:
        err = -0.5
    P = Kp * err
    if P > 0.35:
        P = 0.35
    if P < -0.35:
        P = -0.35
    i_prop = i_prev + Ki * err * dt
    i_prop = _clip(i_prop, -INT_LIM, INT_LIM)
    u_test = ff + P + i_prop
    integ = i_prop
    if (u_test > U_MAX and err > 0.0) or (u_test < 0.0 and err < 0.0):
        integ = i_prev
    u = ff + P + integ
    u = _clip(u, 0.0, U_MAX)
    if u_prev is not None and math.isfinite(u_prev):
        max_step = 0.10 + 0.03 * dt
        du = u - u_prev
        if du > max_step:
            u = u_prev + max_step
        elif du < -max_step:
            u = u_prev - max_step
    u = _clip(u, 0.0, 1.0)
    if not math.isfinite(u):
        u = ff
        integ = i_prev
    new_state = {"yf": float(yf), "i": float(integ), "u": float(u)}
    return (float(u), new_state)
"
}

{
  "change_summary": "Kept proven PI+feedforward+filter core but made steady-state gain adaptive. Added online K estimator (Kest init 1.32, adapted only when filtered output-rate and input are settled) driving ff=(target-AMB)/Kest, raised fast-integral authority from 0.15 to 0.20 with Ki 0.007->0.008, kept U_MAX 0.70 and rate limiter. This directly targets ~45% loss of heater gain while leaving nominal dynamics, filtering, and safety clamps unchanged.",
  "design_rationale": "Zero-input decays E2 vs E8 are identical (0.469->0.147 vs 0.41->0.157, same shape/time) so loss coefficient/ambient unchanged; response starts in 16-40 s both eras so no extra delay; same u=0.4 gives ~0.54 and still rising pre vs ~0.40-0.44 flattening post, and u=0.55 only reaches ~0.50 post vs ~0.89 predicted pre. That is weaker actuator, not faster outflow. Fixed ff=0.265 can no longer hold 0.5 (needs ~0.48) and INT_LIM 0.15 caps at ~0.465 including P, explaining monitoring MAE 0.015->0.046 with y stuck ~0.45 while u saturates slowly at 0.40. A larger fixed ff would break nominal; therefore estimate K online from settled (yf-AMB)/uf and recompute ff, with fast PI for transients. Gating on |dy/dt|<0.0008/s, uf in [0.12,0.75], yf in [0.20,0.85], |u-uf|<0.10 and tauK=150 s rejects transients and +/-0.03 noise. Bounds Kest [0.55,1.60] => ff [0.22,0.64] keep u<0.70 safe; fast I handles remainder.",
  "diagnosis": "Actuator gain fell ~45%: pre K=(yss-0.15)/u ~1.27-1.40 (0.33->0.571, 0.27->0.527, 0.26->0.483, 0.25->0.466) with ambient ~0.15 and tau ~120-180 s; post K'~0.70-0.75 (0.4->~0.44 from E9 0.174->0.406 in 270 s flattening, 0.55->~0.55 from E10 0.417->0.496 in 130 s, 0.48->0.547 in E11) with same ambient 0.157 and same u=0 decay shape/time as E2, and same 10-40 s initial response. Hence same input now produces ~0.55x temperature rise, decay at zero input unchanged, delay unchanged, sensor scatter/ambient unchanged. Old ff=0.265 + max I 0.15 cannot supply new u*~0.48, leaving ~0.05 steady error as seen in monitoring after-change trace y~0.45 at u~0.40 and climbing only 0.0007/s.",
  "diagnosis_category": "actuator_weaker",
  "machine_card": "First-order heater y in [0,1] (0.15 ambient). Pre: yss=0.15+1.32*u, tau ~150 s, deadtime <30 s, u* (0.5)=0.265, noise +/-0.03 with 0.05-0.08 outliers. Post: yss=0.157+0.71*u (range 0.68-0.82 given 110-270 s settles), tau ~120-180 s unchanged, deadtime tens of s unchanged, ambient ~0.15-0.16 unchanged, u*(0.5)=0.47-0.50 (twin needing ~0.375 implies K'~0.93 in that twin; design covers 0.55-1.60), no deadzone, soft limit 0.85 / hard 0.9 unchanged.",
  "operator_note": "Drop-in replacement, same interface. No tuning needed: starts at nominal gain 1.32 and learns lower gain automatically in ~3-5 min when settled. Expect higher steady power (~0.38-0.50 vs 0.27) on degraded heater and ~40% higher energy; this is required physics. Safe: output clamped [0,0.70] with rate limit, filtered for noise/outliers, handles NaN/inf/dt faults. If sensor or delay changes instead, adaptation freezes (rate/input-settled gate) and fast PI still controls.",
  "predicted_behavior": "Nominal: Kest stays ~1.30, ff~0.265, MAE ~0.025, in-band ~0.76 after 300 s, energy ~130, zero overrides as before. Degraded (K'~0.7): Kest converges 1.32->~0.72 in ~300 s, ff 0.265->~0.48, y rises without overshoot >0.70, settles 0.475-0.525 by ~300-400 s, residual MAE ~0.014-0.020, in-band ~0.76-0.78, energy ~185-195 due to higher u, zero hard violations/overrides. If diagnosis wrong (faster loss), Kest still moves to match observed (yf-AMB)/u and integral covers remainder, so no worse than v1.",
  "self_test_expectations": [
    "cold start y=0.15 target 0.5 returns u ~0.60-0.65 finite and state has yf,i,u,K~1.32,uf",
    "50 consecutive steps with dt 3-6 s all finite in [0,0.70] and deterministic repeat",
    "NaN/inf y returns finite u using last yf and survives next valid step",
    "dt 0 or negative defaults to 5 s and remains finite",
    "settled at y=0.50 u=0.27 keeps Kest 1.2-1.4 and ff 0.24-0.29",
    "settled at y=0.45 u=0.40 drives Kest down toward 0.65-0.85 and ff up toward 0.42-0.55 within ~300 s",
    "u=0 decay curve unchanged: no K update during large |dy/dt| transient"
  ],
  "source_code": "import math
def _clip(x, lo, hi):
    if x < lo:
        return lo
    if x > hi:
        return hi
    return x
def control(obs, state):
    AMB = 0.15
    G0 = 1.32
    Kp = 1.0
    Ki = 0.008
    TAU_F = 22.0
    TAU_U = 60.0
    TAU_K = 150.0
    INT_LIM = 0.20
    U_MAX = 0.70
    K_MIN = 0.55
    K_MAX = 1.60
    try:
